IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-approval-loans.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 4: Transactions with directors requiring approval of
-- members: "Loans, quasi-loans and credit transactions" (ss 197 to 203) and the first subsections of s 204 (exception for expenditure
-- on company business), lines 2569-2696 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Section 204(2) is the last line of
-- this part's range; the next section, s 205, is coa5's, as are ss 205 to 209 (the other exceptions): their effect is one input.
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4 and coa4-approval-service-property.l4 (the bar functions: JUST TRUE =
-- the section bars the company, JUST FALSE = it does not, NOTHING = outside the subsection's own wording or a borrowed answer is not
-- known). Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 197: loans to directors: requirement of members' approval ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2581 | (4) The matters to be disclosed are—
-- src:2582 | (a) the nature of the transaction,
-- src:2583 | (b) the amount of the loan and the purpose for which it is required, and
-- src:2584 | (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the loan.
@ref s 197(4) Matters to be disclosed (src:2581-2584)
GIVEN `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the amount of the loan and the purpose for which it is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(4) the memorandum sets out the matters to be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the amount of the loan and the purpose for which it is required`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the loan`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters to be disclosed are— (a) the nature of the transaction, (b) the amount of the loan and the purpose for which it is required, and (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the loan."

GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(3) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution approving a transaction to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (4) is made available to members"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution`
              THEN IF `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
         OTHERWISE IF       ((Day `the day of the meeting` MINUS Day `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office`) PLUS 1) AT LEAST 15
                      AND `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"


GIVEN `s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company`)) OR `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when no approval is required on the part of the members of a body corporate

-- src:2570 | 197 Loans to directors: requirement of members' approval
-- src:2571 | (1) A company may not—
-- src:2572 | (a) make a loan to a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:2573 | (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan made by any person to such a director,
-- src:2574 | unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 197(1) Loans to directors: requirement of members' approval (src:2570-2574)
GIVEN `the company makes a loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan made by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(1) section 197(1) bars the company from the transaction` MEANS
    IF NOT ((`the company makes a loan` OR `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan made by any person`) AND `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may not— (a) make a loan to a director of the company or of its holding company, or (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan made by any person to such a director"
    ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
         ELSE IF `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company"
              ELSE IF `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2575 | (2) If the director is a director of the company's holding company, the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 197(2) The members of the holding company (src:2575)
GIVEN `the director is a director of the company's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 197(2) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director is a director of the company's holding company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the director is a director of the company's holding company"
    ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
         ELSE IF `s 197(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 198: quasi-loans to directors: requirement of members' approval ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2602 | (5) The matters to be disclosed are—
-- src:2603 | (a) the nature of the transaction,
-- src:2604 | (b) the amount of the quasi-loan and the purpose for which it is required, and
-- src:2605 | (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the quasi-loan.
@ref s 198(5) Matters to be disclosed (src:2602-2605)
GIVEN `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the amount of the quasi-loan and the purpose for which it is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(5) the memorandum sets out the matters to be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the amount of the quasi-loan and the purpose for which it is required`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the quasi-loan`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters to be disclosed are— (a) the nature of the transaction, (b) the amount of the quasi-loan and the purpose for which it is required, and (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the quasi-loan."

GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(4) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (5)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution approving a transaction to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (5) is made available to members"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution`
              THEN IF `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
         OTHERWISE IF       ((Day `the day of the meeting` MINUS Day `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office`) PLUS 1) AT LEAST 15
                      AND `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"


GIVEN `s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company`)) OR `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when no approval is required on the part of the members of a body corporate

-- src:2588 | 198 Quasi-loans to directors: requirement of members' approval
-- src:2589 | (1) This section applies to a company if it is—
-- src:2590 | (a) a public company, or
-- src:2591 | (b) a company associated with a public company.
@ref s 198(1) Companies to which the section applies (src:2588-2591)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 256 the company is associated with a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(1) the section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 256 the company is associated with a public company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a company if it is— (a) a public company, or (b) a company associated with a public company."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is associated with a public company is s 256 (coa5)

-- src:2592 | (2) A company to which this section applies may not—
-- src:2593 | (a) make a quasi-loan to a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:2594 | (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a quasi-loan made by any person to such a director,
-- src:2595 | unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 198(2) Quasi-loans to directors: requirement of members' approval (src:2592-2595)
GIVEN `the answer under s 198(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company makes a quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a quasi-loan made by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 198(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(2) the section bars the company from the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under s 198(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this section applies may not"; the section does not apply to this company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the company is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF NOT ((`the company makes a quasi-loan` OR `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a quasi-loan made by any person`) AND `the borrower is a director of the company or of its holding company`)
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company to which this section applies may not— (a) make a quasi-loan to a director of the company or of its holding company, or (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a quasi-loan made by any person to such a director"
             ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
                  ELSE IF `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval`
                       THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company"
                       ELSE IF `s 198(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
                            ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2596 | (3) If the director is a director of the company's holding company, the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 198(3) The members of the holding company (src:2596)
GIVEN `the director is a director of the company's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 198(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 198(3) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director is a director of the company's holding company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the director is a director of the company's holding company"
    ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
         ELSE IF `s 198(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 199: meaning of "quasi-loan" and related expressions ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2609 | 199 Meaning of “quasi-loan” and related expressions
-- src:2610 | (1) A “quasi-loan” is a transaction under which one party (“the creditor”) agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, a sum for another (“the borrower”) or agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another (“the borrower”)—
-- src:2611 | (a) on terms that the borrower (or a person on his behalf) will reimburse the creditor; or
-- src:2612 | (b) in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor.
@ref s 199(1) Quasi-loan (src:2609-2612)
GIVEN `one party (the creditor) agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, a sum for another (the borrower)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one party (the creditor) agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another (the borrower)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on terms that the borrower (or a person on his behalf) will reimburse the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(1) the transaction is a quasi-loan` MEANS
    IF       (`one party (the creditor) agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, a sum for another (the borrower)` OR `one party (the creditor) agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another (the borrower)`)
         AND (`it is on terms that the borrower (or a person on his behalf) will reimburse the creditor` OR `it is in circumstances giving rise to a liability on the borrower to reimburse the creditor`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “quasi-loan” is a transaction under which one party (“the creditor”) agrees to pay, or pays otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, a sum for another (“the borrower”) or agrees to reimburse, or reimburses otherwise than in pursuance of an agreement, expenditure incurred by another party for another (“the borrower”)—"

-- src:2613 | (2) Any reference to the person to whom a quasi-loan is made is a reference to the borrower.
@ref s 199(2) The person to whom a quasi-loan is made (src:2613)
GIVEN `the person is the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(2) the person is the person to whom the quasi-loan is made` MEANS
    IF `the person is the borrower`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any reference to the person to whom a quasi-loan is made is a reference to the borrower."

-- src:2614 | (3) The liabilities of the borrower under a quasi-loan include the liabilities of any person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower.
@ref s 199(3) The liabilities of the borrower (src:2614)
GIVEN `the liability is a liability of the borrower under the quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is that of a person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 199(3) the liability is a liability of the borrower under the quasi-loan` MEANS
    IF `the liability is a liability of the borrower under the quasi-loan` OR `the liability is that of a person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The liabilities of the borrower under a quasi-loan include the liabilities of any person who has agreed to reimburse the creditor on behalf of the borrower."

