    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution approving a transaction to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (5) is made available to members"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution`
              THEN IF `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
         OTHERWISE IF       ((Day `the day of the meeting` MINUS Day `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office`) PLUS 1) AT LEAST 15
                      AND `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"


GIVEN `s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company`)) OR `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when no approval is required on the part of the members of a body corporate

-- src:2615 | 200 Loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors: requirement of members' approval
-- src:2616 | (1) This section applies to a company if it is—
-- src:2617 | (a) a public company, or
-- src:2618 | (b) a company associated with a public company.
@ref s 200(1) Companies to which the section applies (src:2615-2618)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 256 the company is associated with a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200(1) the section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 256 the company is associated with a public company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a company if it is— (a) a public company, or (b) a company associated with a public company."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is associated with a public company is s 256 (coa5)

-- src:2619 | (2) A company to which this section applies may not—
-- src:2620 | (a) make a loan or quasi-loan to a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company, or
-- src:2621 | (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made by any person to a person connected with such a director,
-- src:2622 | unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 200(2) Loans or quasi-loans to persons connected with directors: requirement of members' approval (src:2619-2622)
GIVEN `the answer under section 200(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company makes a loan or quasi-loan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 252 the borrower is a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 200(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200(2) the section bars the company from the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 200(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this section applies may not"; the section does not apply to this company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the company is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF NOT (`the company makes a loan or quasi-loan` OR `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made by any person`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company to which this section applies may not— (a) make a loan or quasi-loan to a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company, or (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a loan or quasi-loan made by any person to a person connected with such a director"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 252 the borrower is a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person connected with a director of the company or of its holding company"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the borrower is connected with a director is s 252 (coa5)
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                   IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
                   ELSE IF `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval`
                        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company"
                        ELSE IF `s 200(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
                             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2623 | (3) If the connected person is a person connected with a director of the company's holding company, the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 200(3) The members of the holding company (src:2623)
GIVEN `the connected person is a person connected with a director of the company's holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 200(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 200(3) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the connected person is a person connected with a director of the company's holding company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the connected person is a person connected with a director of the company's holding company"
    ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
         ELSE IF `s 200(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 201: credit transactions: requirement of members' approval ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2650 | (5) The matters to be disclosed are—
-- src:2651 | (a) the nature of the transaction,
-- src:2652 | (b) the value of the credit transaction and the purpose for which the land, goods or services sold or otherwise disposed of, leased, hired or supplied under the credit transaction are required, and
-- src:2653 | (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the credit transaction.
@ref s 201(5) Matters to be disclosed (src:2650-2653)
GIVEN `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the value of the credit transaction and the purpose for which the land, goods or services sold or otherwise disposed of, leased, hired or supplied under the credit transaction are required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the credit transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(5) the memorandum sets out the matters to be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the memorandum sets out the nature of the transaction`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the value of the credit transaction and the purpose for which the land, goods or services sold or otherwise disposed of, leased, hired or supplied under the credit transaction are required`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the credit transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters to be disclosed are— (a) the nature of the transaction, (b) the value of the credit transaction and the purpose for which the land, goods or services sold or otherwise disposed of, leased, hired or supplied under the credit transaction are required, and (c) the extent of the company's liability under any transaction connected with the credit transaction."

GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(4) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (5)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution approving a transaction to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (5) is made available to members"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution`
              THEN IF `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
         OTHERWISE IF       ((Day `the day of the meeting` MINUS Day `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office`) PLUS 1) AT LEAST 15
                      AND `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"


GIVEN `s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company`)) OR `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when no approval is required on the part of the members of a body corporate

-- src:2636 | 201 Credit transactions: requirement of members' approval
-- src:2637 | (1) This section applies to a company if it is—
-- src:2638 | (a) a public company, or
-- src:2639 | (b) a company associated with a public company.
@ref s 201(1) Companies to which the section applies (src:2636-2639)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 256 the company is associated with a public company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(1) the section applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 256 the company is associated with a public company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a company if it is— (a) a public company, or (b) a company associated with a public company."
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is associated with a public company is s 256 (coa5)

-- src:2640 | (2) A company to which this section applies may not—
-- src:2641 | (a) enter into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director, or
-- src:2642 | (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of such a director, or a person connected with such a director,
-- src:2643 | unless the transaction (that is, the credit transaction, the giving of the guarantee or the provision of security, as the case may be) has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 201(2) Credit transactions: requirement of members' approval (src:2640-2643)
GIVEN `the answer under section 201(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company enters into a credit transaction as creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 202(1) the transaction is a credit transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the credit transaction is for the benefit of a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 252 the person for whose benefit the credit transaction is entered into is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 201(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(2) the section bars the company from the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 201(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company to which this section applies may not"; the section does not apply to this company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to the company is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF NOT (`the company enters into a credit transaction as creditor` OR `the company gives a guarantee or provides security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company to which this section applies may not— (a) enter into a credit transaction as creditor for the benefit of a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with such a director, or (b) give a guarantee or provide security in connection with a credit transaction entered into by any person for the benefit of such a director, or a person connected with such a director"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 202(1) the transaction is a credit transaction`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a credit transaction"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction is a credit transaction is s 202(1) and the caller's facts
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                   CONSIDER `the benefit party counts`
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the benefit of such a director, or a person connected with such a director"
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is connected with a director is s 252 (coa5)
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
                        IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
                        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the transaction (that is, the credit transaction, the giving of the guarantee or the provision of security, as the case may be) has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
                        ELSE IF `an exception in section 204, 205, 206, 207, 208 or 209 disapplies the requirement of approval`
                             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company"
                             ELSE IF `s 201(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
                                  ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the benefit party counts` MEANS
            IF `the credit transaction is for the benefit of a director of the company or of its holding company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE `s 252 the person for whose benefit the credit transaction is entered into is connected with a director of the company or of its holding company`

-- src:2644 | (3) If the director or connected person is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director, the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 201(3) The members of the holding company (src:2644)
GIVEN `the director or connected person is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 201(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201(3) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director or connected person is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the director or connected person is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director"
    ELSE IF `the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transaction must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
         ELSE IF `s 201(6) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 202: meaning of "credit transaction" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2657 | 202 Meaning of “credit transaction”
-- src:2658 | (1) A “credit transaction” is a transaction under which one party (“the creditor”)—
-- src:2659 | (a) supplies any goods or sells any land under a hire-purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement,
-- src:2660 | (b) leases or hires any land or goods in return for periodical payments, or
-- src:2661 | (c) otherwise disposes of land or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment (whether in a lump sum or instalments or by way of periodical payments or otherwise) is to be deferred.
@ref s 202(1) Credit transaction (src:2657-2661)
GIVEN `the creditor supplies any goods or sells any land under a hire-purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor leases or hires any land or goods in return for periodical payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creditor otherwise disposes of land or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment (whether in a lump sum or instalments or by way of periodical payments or otherwise) is to be deferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the transaction is a credit transaction` MEANS
    IF       `the creditor supplies any goods or sells any land under a hire-purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement`
         OR  `the creditor leases or hires any land or goods in return for periodical payments`
         OR  `the creditor otherwise disposes of land or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment (whether in a lump sum or instalments or by way of periodical payments or otherwise) is to be deferred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “credit transaction” is a transaction under which one party (“the creditor”)— (a) supplies any goods or sells any land under a hire-purchase agreement or a conditional sale agreement, (b) leases or hires any land or goods in return for periodical payments, or (c) otherwise disposes of land or supplies goods or services on the understanding that payment (whether in a lump sum or instalments or by way of periodical payments or otherwise) is to be deferred."

-- src:2662 | (2) Any reference to the person for whose benefit a credit transaction is entered into is to the person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction.
@ref s 202(2) The person for whose benefit a credit transaction is entered into (src:2662)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(2) the person is the person for whose benefit the credit transaction is entered into` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any reference to the person for whose benefit a credit transaction is entered into is to the person to whom goods, land or services are supplied, sold, leased, hired or otherwise disposed of under the transaction."

-- src:2663 | (3) In this section—
-- src:2664 | “conditional sale agreement” has the same meaning as in the Consumer Credit Act 1974 (c. 39); and
@ref s 202(3) "conditional sale agreement" (src:2663-2664)
GIVEN `the agreement is a conditional sale agreement as defined in the Consumer Credit Act 1974` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(3) the agreement is a conditional sale agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the agreement is a conditional sale agreement as defined in the Consumer Credit Act 1974`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“conditional sale agreement” has the same meaning as in the Consumer Credit Act 1974"; the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the borrowed definition is in the Consumer Credit Act 1974

-- src:2663 | (3) In this section—
-- src:2665 | “services” means anything other than goods or land.
@ref s 202(3) "services" (src:2663 and src:2665)
GIVEN `the thing is goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(3) the thing is services` MEANS
    IF `the thing is goods` OR `the thing is land`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“services” means anything other than goods or land."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

