-- src:2679 | (4) The matters to be disclosed are—
-- src:2680 | (a) the matters that would have to be disclosed if the company were seeking approval of the transaction to which the arrangement relates,
-- src:2681 | (b) the nature of the arrangement, and
-- src:2682 | (c) the extent of the company's liability under the arrangement or any transaction connected with it.
@ref s 203(4) Matters to be disclosed (src:2679-2682)
GIVEN `the memorandum sets out the matters that would have to be disclosed if the company were seeking approval of the transaction to which the arrangement relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the nature of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under the arrangement or any transaction connected with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(4) the memorandum sets out the matters to be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the memorandum sets out the matters that would have to be disclosed if the company were seeking approval of the transaction to which the arrangement relates`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the nature of the arrangement`
         AND `the memorandum sets out the extent of the company's liability under the arrangement or any transaction connected with it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters to be disclosed are— (a) the matters that would have to be disclosed if the company were seeking approval of the transaction to which the arrangement relates, (b) the nature of the arrangement, and (c) the extent of the company's liability under the arrangement or any transaction connected with it."

GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(3) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the memorandum sets out the matters mentioned in subsection (4)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution approving an arrangement to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out the matters mentioned in subsection (4) is made available to members"
    ELSE CONSIDER way
         WHEN `as a written resolution`
              THEN IF `the memorandum was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
         OTHERWISE IF       ((Day `the day of the meeting` MINUS Day `the first day on which the memorandum was available for inspection at the company's registered office`) PLUS 1) AT LEAST 15
                      AND `the memorandum was available for inspection at the meeting itself`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by members of the company both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"


GIVEN `s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 1158 the body corporate is a UK-registered company`)) OR `s 1159(2) the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when no approval is required on the part of the members of a body corporate

-- src:2686 | (6) In determining for the purposes of this section whether a transaction is one that would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 if it had been entered into by the company, the transaction shall be treated as having been entered into on the date of the arrangement.
@ref s 203(6) The date of the arrangement (src:2686)
GIVEN `the question is whether a transaction is one that would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 if it had been entered into by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the arrangement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 203(6) the date on which the transaction is treated as having been entered into` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether a transaction is one that would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 if it had been entered into by the company`
    THEN JUST `the date of the arrangement`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining for the purposes of this section whether a transaction is one that would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 if it had been entered into by the company"

-- src:2667 | (1) A company may not—
-- src:2668 | (a) take part in an arrangement under which—
-- src:2669 | (i) another person enters into a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201, and
-- src:2670 | (ii) that person, in pursuance of the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a body corporate associated with it, or
-- src:2671 | (b) arrange for the assignment to it, or assumption by it, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required such approval,
-- src:2672 | unless the arrangement in question has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 203(1) Related arrangements: requirement of members' approval (src:2667-2672)
GIVEN `the company takes part in an arrangement under which another person enters into a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that person, in pursuance of the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a body corporate associated with it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company arranges for the assignment to it, or assumption by it, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required such approval` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement in question has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(1) section 203(1) bars the company from the arrangement` MEANS
    IF       (    `the company takes part in an arrangement under which another person enters into a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `that person, in pursuance of the arrangement, obtains a benefit from the company or a body corporate associated with it`)
         OR  `the company arranges for the assignment to it, or assumption by it, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required such approval` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the arrangement in question has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the arrangement in question has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
         ELSE IF `s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the company takes part in an arrangement under which another person enters into a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the company arranges for the assignment to it, or assumption by it, of any rights, obligations or liabilities under a transaction that, if it had been entered into by the company, would have required such approval` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction would have required approval under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 is those sections' answer, which the caller has not given
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may not— (a) take part in an arrangement under which"; the arrangement is not within the subsection

-- src:2673 | (2) If the director or connected person for whom the transaction is entered into is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director, the arrangement must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company.
@ref s 203(2) The members of the holding company (src:2673)
GIVEN `the director or connected person for whom the transaction is entered into is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangement has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 203(2) the section requires the approval of the members of the holding company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the director or connected person for whom the transaction is entered into is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the director or connected person for whom the transaction is entered into is a director of its holding company or a person connected with such a director"
    ELSE IF `the arrangement has been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the arrangement must also have been approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company"
         ELSE IF `s 203(5) approval is required on the part of the members of the holding company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 204: exception for expenditure on company business --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:2687 | 204 Exception for expenditure on company business
-- src:2688 | (1) Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company—
-- src:2689 | (a) to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him—
-- src:2690 | (i) for the purposes of the company, or
-- src:2691 | (ii) for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company, or
-- src:2692 | (b) to enable any such person to avoid incurring such expenditure.
@ref s 204(1) Exception for expenditure on company business (src:2687-2692)
GIVEN `the thing done by the company is to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purposes of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing done by the company is to provide such a person with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing done by the company is to enable such a person to avoid incurring such expenditure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(1) approval is required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 for the thing done` MEANS
    IF       `the thing done by the company is to provide a director of the company or of its holding company, or a person connected with any such director, with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purposes of the company`
         OR  `the thing done by the company is to provide such a person with funds to meet expenditure incurred or to be incurred by him for the purpose of enabling him properly to perform his duties as an officer of the company`
         OR  `the thing done by the company is to enable such a person to avoid incurring such expenditure`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Approval is not required under section 197, 198, 200 or 201 (requirement of members' approval for loans etc) for anything done by a company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only for which things approval is not required

-- src:2693 | (2) This section does not authorise a company to enter into a transaction if the aggregate of—
-- src:2694 | (a) the value of the transaction in question, and
-- src:2695 | (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements,
-- src:2696 | exceeds £50,000.
@ref s 204(2) The limit of 50,000 pounds (src:2693-2696)
GIVEN `the value of the transaction in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(2) section 204 authorises the company to enter into the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the value of the transaction in question` PLUS `the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements` GREATER THAN 50000
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not authorise a company to enter into a transaction if the aggregate of— (a) the value of the transaction in question, and (b) the value of any other relevant transactions or arrangements, exceeds £50,000."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when the section does not authorise a transaction
